WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.801 --> 00:00:07.443
This is AZM SPARK, an AI fitness coach that adapts to your medical condition, using only a phone camera.

2
00:00:11.109 --> 00:00:15.059
Anyone can start from the home page. No app, and no account.

3
00:00:16.517 --> 00:00:18.509
First, choose how you train.

4
00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.855
Then prop up the phone, about two meters away.

5
00:00:28.258 --> 00:00:34.114
Coach: Welcome to Azm. Move at your own pace, within your comfortable range.

6
00:00:34.983 --> 00:00:41.103
Coach: Let’s find your range. Repeat the movement slowly, at a comfortable effort.

7
00:00:42.418 --> 00:00:44.578
Coach: 1

8
00:00:45.051 --> 00:00:45.951
Coach: 2

9
00:00:47.553 --> 00:00:51.801
Coach: Steady your trunk. Adjust your sitting position.

10
00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:56.197
Coach: 5

11
00:00:56.449 --> 00:00:58.360
Then the person rates the effort.

12
00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:04.614
The summary separates clean reps from compensated ones.

13
00:01:09.954 --> 00:01:12.457
A free account keeps everything together.

14
00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:18.945
Now the medical engine. Paste or photograph a medical report.

15
00:01:23.157 --> 00:01:29.997
Azm fills in the profile from the report, and asks only what is missing. The report is never stored.

16
00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:36.318
Safety questions are always answered by the person, never guessed.

17
00:01:39.574 --> 00:01:43.847
Nothing is built until the person reviews and consents.

18
00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:49.624
Clinical rules set a safe dose for this condition.

19
00:01:54.109 --> 00:01:58.835
Then AI writes the week, using only exercises the rules approved.

20
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.517
Every day is laid out, and the plan explains why it fits.

21
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.460
And it explains why the plan fits.

22
00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:14.988
Now, add a heart condition.

23
00:02:22.738 --> 00:02:29.069
SPARK stops, shows the reasons, and asks for a clinical review instead of a workout.

24
00:02:31.577 --> 00:02:37.284
AZM SPARK. Training is still yours, whatever your body has been through.
